@mislav my intent was to only show colored labels in both `gh pr view` and `gh issue view`. 

Something I maybe should have noted in #3912 was that I only had to change `view.go` for the `pr` colored labels to work. Whereas with `issues` I had to change `display.go`, which I now realize is because labels pass through `display.go` for both `view` and `list` for `gh issue`. 

Sorry for creating the bug, I can look into solutions later today. My question would be, original intent aside, do you think it would be better to have colored labels in `gh issue list` or would it be best to only display colored labels in `gh issue view`

@bchadwic Thanks for taking a look! Personally, I wouldn't extend the functionality to `gh issue view` just yet. The rationale is that the readability of the text that varies in color is dependent on the background that it's displayed on. For example, I created some very dark labels in my test repo, and here's how it looks on a dark background:

<img width="383" alt="" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/887/128001747-c523e651-188d-4af9-8335-870d9bb20f69.png">

You can see that `help wanted gh` and `duplicate` labels are barely legible. GitHub web interface compensates for text color by automatically choosing a background color that has sufficient contrast when combined together. So does `hub`, an older CLI for GitHub: https://github.com/github/hub/blob/c8e68d548a39ec0fab6f674a669c21b54d4eec61/commands/issue.go#L791-L796
